# Public EKS access is enabled by default to simplify local development and testing.
# For production environments, set `eks_endpoint_public_access = false` and
# restrict `eks_public_access_cidrs` to specific CIDRs.
AVD-AWS-0040
AVD-AWS-0041

# Public subnets with auto-assign public IP are used intentionally in some examples.
# For production, use private subnets or set `map_public_ip_on_launch = false`.
AVD-AWS-0164

# Unrestricted egress on the node/cluster security groups comes from the upstream
# terraform-aws-modules/eks defaults (egress_all) and is required for image pulls,
# the EKS API endpoint, and ECR/S3 access. Not patchable from this module.
AVD-AWS-0104

# Secrets envelope encryption is opt-in via `eks_enable_secrets_encryption`;
# enabling it by default would create a KMS key and change behavior for existing users.
AVD-AWS-0039
